# Builder prefills and input-route overrides (ADR 0009).
#
#   cp .env.example .env    # then edit — .env is gitignored, never commit it
#   tools/build-iso.sh <product>
#
# A plain `nix build .#installer-iso-<product>` ignores .env entirely (pure
# evaluation) and builds the tracked defaults. Values here may only change
# what an installer PREFILLS or displays, and where input bytes are fetched
# from — never anything that reaches the Target, and never a gate
# (Reachability probe, disko and Pin-match confirmations). See
# CONTEXT-MAP.md: Builder prefill.

# The Cache URL the proxied installers prefill (docs/proxied/CONTEXT.md:
# Cache URL) — a Nix substituter base URL, never an http_proxy value. The
# operator still confirms it behind the Reachability probe.
#ISO_CACHE_URL=http://my-nix-cache.lan

# Reroute flake-input FETCHES for cold builds behind a Cache proxy:
# space-separated input=url pairs, each handed to --override-input.
# IMPORTANT: an override REPLACES the input's lock entry — append
# ?narHash=<the hash from your committed flake.lock> so the fetched content
# stays pinned to what the lock recorded (the route changes, the bytes
# don't). tools/build-iso.sh warns on any override without a narHash.
# This file is read in a clean environment: static KEY=VALUE lines only,
# no references to other variables.
#ISO_INPUT_OVERRIDES="determinate=tarball+http://my-nix-cache.lan/flakehub/f/DeterminateSystems/determinate/3.21.9.tar.gz?narHash=sha256-IrqJV%2B9NcFevwyBBqEkxkbqhX3rtJI7sSzHz5wDVaLo%3D"
